WEBVTT

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.250
Well,

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:16.120
what did you think of
Death Voice Channel's second episode?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.120
If you still can't use your death voice,
just be patient and keep practicing.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.330
If you liked the video,
please click this button to subscribe!

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.000
What...?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.700
RAGE

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.040
You sure took your time in the restroom.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.620
I've connected my smartphone
to the karaoke machine.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:53.040
I see.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.750
What are you doing?

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.410
I'm searching for our songs.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.660
You won't find them there.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.500
I don't remember
signing a karaoke contract.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.000
Well, I know that.

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.950
I was just checking.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.750
Do you know how many songs are in here?

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:15.910
No idea.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.160
270,000 songs.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.910
So even if our new song gets registered,

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.080
it'll still be the 270,001st song.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.750
It's like dropping a grain of sand
in the desert.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.870
How can we avoid being buried?

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.410
We have no choice but to find a weapon,
some way to make us stand out.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.410
A weapon?

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.000
I'll think of something.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.790
Wait, where are you going?
What about practice?

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.790
I changed my mind.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.250
There's no practice today.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.080
What? What do you mean? Hey, wait!

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.950
Ms. Washimi.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:12.040
Come here a sec, please.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.410
Here you go.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.080
What's this?

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:19.370
It's the money I borrowed.
It really came in handy.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:20.700
Thank you so much!

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.660
What's with all the secrecy?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.870
If Ms. Gori finds out I talked to you
about this, and not her,

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.370
it could become a problem.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.450
Ah, you're right.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.450
She'd probably say something like,
"Why didn't you come to me?"

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.410
Whoa, you sound exactly like her!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.450
We're friends for a reason.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.500
Good morning!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.500
Ms. Gori...

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.080
Good morning.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.000
What are you girls doing?

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:49.040
Um, we're, uh...

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.040
How should I say this?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.290
We were talking about
how we miss going out as a group.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.910
Huh? Are we planning a trip?
Where are we going?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.290
We haven't decided anything.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.700
Anyway, how's the side hustle? Busy?

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.040
Ugh, yes! Just listen to this!

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.500
That app...

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.250
Thank you, everyone!

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.160
I love you all!

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.200
You're going to release a new song?

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.410
Yes! We're working on it now.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.660
I'll buy ten CDs when it's out.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.290
I'll buy 100!

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.200
I'll buy 1,000!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.330
-10,000!
-I'll buy 100,000!

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.330
I'll do my best to sell a million!

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:01.040
Um...

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.700
What is this?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.450
That's OTM Girls' new song.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.700
The guitar is so noisy
and the bass drum is nuts.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.080
This is a totally different song
to the demo you gave me.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:20.040
I asked the composer to remake it.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:25.000
Releasing a new song is like dropping
a grain of sand in the desert.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.580
What does one need to drop
to guarantee it won't be buried?

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.870
A... Uh, a gemstone!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.160
Impossible.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:34.370
You'd need both money
and incredible talent.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.660
A pebble?

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.290
Unmemorable.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:39.750
What about, for example...

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:42.750
-A sea urchin.
-A sea urchin?

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.250
You'd be shocked
if you saw one in the desert, right?

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.410
Well, you have a point.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.660
I'll remove Manaka
from the center position.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:53.080
The lead vocalist will be a new member.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.950
A new member?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.040
Wait a minute. This is absurd!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.290
Manaka has practiced so hard.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.830
It's so mean of you
to just change it up like that!

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.790
Besides,
where would you find a new member?

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.870
Are you going to start looking now?

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.330
I've already found her.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.540
Where did you find...

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:23.790
The main vocalist for the new song,
accounting manager,

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.290
is you.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.830
<i>What...?</i>

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.250
He caught you singing death metal
in a karaoke booth?

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.700
Yeah, I guess he just happened to see me.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:42.040
So, what are you going to do?
Will you do it?

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.910
Oh, come on!
I turned him down on the spot.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.950
Why?

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.080
What? Well, you know, I'm already 25.

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.950
I'm too old to become an idol.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.370
That doesn't matter.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:54.910
Yes, it does!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.120
There's no way I can sing like that
in front of people!

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.410
Good morning!

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.370
Oh, Ms. Gori!

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.700
Good morning!

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.200
What are you girls chatting about?

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.620
We were, um...

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.700
We were talking about
how we miss going out as a group.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.200
Ah...

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.120
Is that so?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.870
I've definitely told you already!

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:28.830
Sorry, sorry.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:33.660
Good morning.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.370
Uh, morning...

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.330
BREAK ROOM

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.790
She's from General Affairs.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.370
Man, giving work advice sure is tiring!

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.830
I see.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:52.700
Yeah.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.580
Do people normally go to you for advice?

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.290
Yeah, that's right!

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.660
I think junior workers
find me rather approachable.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.580
Hey, can I ask you something weird?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.870
Yeah, sure.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:11.790
Let's say...

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.950
you have a hobby that
you don't want people to know about,

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:18.450
but there's someone
who really appreciates it,

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.250
and that person asks you to perform
your hobby in front of people.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.620
Uh-huh...

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.540
What would you do?

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.040
This is all a bit vague.
I'm not sure what to say.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.080
Is this about you?

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:34.290
Did something happen?

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.950
What? No! Not me!

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.660
It's just a hypothetical question.
What do you think?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.000
It depends...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.120
Thought so.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.160
So this is a story about my friend...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.080
Okay.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:55.410
He really likes this girl, girl A,
but girl A isn't interested.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.370
Ah, unrequited love.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:03.120
On the other hand,
there's this other girl, girl B,

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.870
who is actively trying
to get closer to my friend.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.790
She's really nice, you know.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:10.700
Gotcha.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.830
What would you do in this situation?

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:17.790
If I had to put myself
in this guy's shoes?

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.790
Yeah.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:24.000
Hmm. I might go out with girl B.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.450
But would I regret it later?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.410
I'm not sure.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:30.950
Well...

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.660
it depends...

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:34.290
Right?

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:58.120
-Did something happen to Retsuko?
-Did something happen to Retsuko?

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.500
She's always acting so secretive.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.250
Isn't she? She's so secretive.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.500
She's been acting kind of strange
for a while now.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.830
She looked like she wanted
to ask me something the other day.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.160
Why didn't I notice?

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.200
Why don't you just ask Washimi?

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.450
The two of them seem to be quite close.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:28.120
Absolutely not!

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.250
If I ask her, she'll just say,

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.620
"What, don't you know?

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.660
But what does it matter?
It's not our business, anyway."

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.540
Was that your Washimi impression?
You sound just like her.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.750
We're friends for a reason!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.870
The trick is to talk as if you haven't
an ounce of blood in your body.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:47.790
Ah...

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.620
Bring all of this inside.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.620
Okay.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.000
Mr. Hyodo?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.620
I'm sorry about the other day...

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.500
About turning down your offer.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:09.080
It was very kind of you.

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.200
Don't worry about that.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.870
That's you, isn't it?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.660
It popped up immediately
after a basic search.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.410
You might be trying to hide your face,
but it's pretty obvious.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.950
You look so happy singing like that.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.330
Why did you turn down the offer?

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.080
Huh?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.120
You felt bad for me, didn't you?

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.500
That upsets me way more, so stop it.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.700
It's not like that.
I'm just not cut out for it.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.500
I have no interest in singing
in front of people.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:56.870
That doesn't make any sense.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:00.120
Why do you go to karaoke
and upload videos, then?

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.450
You're expressing yourself.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.450
That means
you have the desire to do it, after all.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:07.950
What? That's not it.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:10.330
I upload them because I need money.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.500
I'm after the ad revenue.

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.790
All right, all right. I get it.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.790
You're a serious good girl.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.540
What?

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.540
That's why you always
have to lay the groundwork.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.580
You need a reason to do things.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.290
You only do something
once you've created a scenario

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.950
where it's seemingly unavoidable,
like needing ad revenue.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.750
Hey, Manaka,

00:12:33.410 --> 00:12:35.750
the thing is, I'm already 25.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.450
I'm too old to be an idol.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.080
Sorry for being too old, then.

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:40.750
Huh?

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.620
I'm 26 years old.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.660
What?

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:52.040
I don't need to apologize to anyone
for being an idol.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.620
I'm doing this because I want to.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.910
I haven't fallen so low
that I need sympathy

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.160
from a subservient woman like you.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:06.160
OTM!

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:09.450
Thank you for an amazing night, everyone!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:12.080
Tonight, we have a special gift

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.580
for all of our supporters.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:17.790
Do you feel burned out?

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:20.830
Life is full of crap, isn't it?

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:24.750
Today, for those of you
who feel that way,

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:27.950
we're dropping a sea urchin
in the desert!

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.120
A sea urchin?

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:33.000
All right,

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.540
this is our new song,

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:36.950
"Aggressive Girl."

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:48.200
Isn't this the remade version?

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.870
We have to change it back!

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.500
We'll continue with this.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:52.830
What?

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.410
I'm not changing the song.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.540
If you don't sing,
this performance will be a disaster.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.250
It's as simple as that.

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:00.700
What are you saying?

00:14:00.790 --> 00:14:02.330
I'm betting on a particular outcome.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:04.410
The rest is up to you.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:05.950
Do as you please.

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.080
<i>What is he saying?</i>

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.120
<i>How can he be so selfish?</i>

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.830
<i>How? Why?</i>

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.910
Hey, the intro is ending.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.290
RAGE

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.160
<i>What's the point</i>
<i>Of trying to be a good girl?!</i>

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.830
<i>I'll get stepped on</i>
<i>By the foot of this crap world</i>

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.080
<i>If you're hearing this</i>
<i>And you wanna gaslight me</i>

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.830
<i>Go ahead an' do it, dick!</i>
<i>Step! Up! Fight! Me!</i>

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.080
<i>See?</i>

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.370
<i>Everyone is appalled.</i>

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.410
<i>You can't use just any old weapon,</i>
<i>you know.</i>

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:56.040
That's right. Let it out. Scream!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.250
And never forget this day.

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:02.700
Let out the roar
that comes from deep within you!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.250
This marks the birth
of "Aggressive Retsuko!"

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:07.200
These are her first cries.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.450
Subtitle translation by Rachael Momber
